# Current Issues — Core Game Backlog

Date: 2026-04-27

The CI/CD pipeline, lobby, and infrastructure are in good shape. This
list captures what's still rough about the *game itself* — the things
players notice within the first few minutes of play.

---

## 1. Bot AI is too weak — bots sometimes die to their own bombs

The bot controller exists and bots move/place bombs, but their decision
making is poor: they frequently walk into their own blast radius and
die without a fight. Solo and 1v3 matches feel one-sided.

## 2. Visual identity is weak — textures don't convey a "game" feel

The current art reads as placeholder/programmer-art rather than a
finished game. Tiles, walls, and players need a coherent visual style
so the world looks like a *game* and not a tech demo.

## 3. No sound effects

There is no audio at all — no footsteps, no bomb fuse tick, no
explosion, no UI clicks, no music. Audio is one of the biggest
contributors to "feel" in an arcade game.

## 4. Items and power-ups lack proper artwork

Pickups (bomb-up, fire-up, speed-down) currently render with minimal
art and don't read clearly at a glance. They need distinct, readable
icons consistent with the rest of the visual style.

## 5. Invite button does not work

The Invite button in the waiting room doesn't successfully bring a
friend into the room. Need to investigate the share-link flow and the
CrazyGames invite popup integration.

## 6. CrazyGames SDK integration is incomplete

The CrazyGames SDK is wired up but not yet compliant with their
publishing standards — gameplay events, ad placement, auth, or invite
hooks are not fully meeting their requirements. Needs an audit pass
against the current CrazyGames developer checklist.
